# What must never reach the image, and why.
#
# `COPY . .` copies the build context, and the build context is a developer's
# working directory. Without this file the image ships the test suite, the local
# SQLite databases, and — if one exists — the .env holding real credentials.
# A secret baked into an image layer stays there after the file is deleted in a
# later layer, so this is the only place to stop it.

# Secrets. First on purpose.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Local databases and media. dev.db has real development data in it.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
.local-data/

# Tests and tooling: build-time concerns, and every file is runtime attack
# surface that cannot be used for anything legitimate in production.
tests/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*

# The local virtualenv. The image builds its own from the lockfile; copying this
# one would overwrite it with a developer's machine, dev dependencies included.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Version control and editor state.
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
